  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Voluntary Wildlife Management Rules as a Solution to Unsustainable Bushmeat Hunting by Gabonese Villages</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support a conservation effort in northeastern Gabon by addressing over-hunting of endangered bushmeat species. This project is intended to protect wildlife from unsustainable harvest by engaging local communities to establish wildlife management rules to reduce pressure on wildlife and reduce the availability of commercial bushmeat. Specific activities include: (1) design and implementation of voluntary wildlife management rules in ten villages; (2) monitoring of bushmeat availability in experimental and control villages; (3) community interviews to determine the effectiveness of wildlife management rules; (4) testing and implementation of wildlife monitoring techniques; (5) community collaboration and hands-on training to develop a conservation ethic among local communities in the Ivindo-Minkb landscape.</narrative>
  </description>
